wip/agentcc-gateway: Import agentcc-gateway-1.54.0

Agent Command Center (agentcc-gateway) is a high-performance,
OpenAI-compatible LLM gateway written in Go. It sits between an
application and LLM providers and gives one OpenAI-compatible API
for every configured provider (OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, Bedrock,
Cohere, Azure, and local endpoints such as vLLM, Ollama and
LocalAI).  It provides routing and failover strategies, caching,
budgets and rate limits, guardrail scanners, and Prometheus and
OpenTelemetry metrics.

Only the gateway is built, from the agentcc-gateway/ subdirectory
of the upstream future-agi monorepo.

The package installs an rc.d script and a minimal agentcc.conf,
which starts the gateway with no providers.  It also installs an
example two-host round-robin/failover config, plus upstream's
config.example.yaml and config.license_auth.example.yaml taken
from the distfile.

Local patches fix biased round-robin and weighted routing when
failover is enabled.  Without them the router was consulted twice
per request.
